    },
    {
      "id": "rY1-4FZ2Dg4jbtbXNUt4l",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 254.55921574043464,
      "y": 512.5,
      "width": 491.8333435058594,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1747145054,
      "version": 3535,
      "versionNonce": 384569950,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791873455946,
      "created": 1791869988858,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How to draw C4 diagrams?\n\n1. Draw a single System box at Context layer\n2. Who is users/actors/roles of the System?\n3. What are surrounding boxes our System interact with?\n4. Put text in boxes, deciphering purpose, responsibility, and\ndescription\n5. Arrows linking boxes are one way (dependency) arrows\n6. Use text to describe arrows\n7. Zoom System box: users, interacting systems retained\n8. Model server side / client side boxes, think in terms of\ndeployable containers. Show Applications, APIs and UIs, Data\nStores (e.g. DB)\n9. Zoom each Container box: draw Components: surrounding\nContainers retained\n\n\n\n*) Note: C4 doesn't limit for notation - it is about abstraction\nlayers. So it's free to use UML or any other notation where\nyou need\n\n*) Layers, Subsystems - modeled by grouping of components.\nSpecifically for huge Monoliths subsystems (Maven modules\ninside Monolith) - are modeled via grouping\n\n*) Note: C4 site has tooling \"Structurizer\" for C4 modelling.\nAnd many modelling cases reviewed on C4 site.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": 24.106006198431025,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "ir8POFS4Aoeh996VKzn4t",
      "originalText": "How to draw C4 diagrams?\n\n1. Draw a single System box at Context layer\n2. Who is users/actors/roles of the System?\n3. What are surrounding boxes our System interact with?\n4. Put text in boxes, deciphering purpose, responsibility, and description\n5. Arrows linking boxes are one way (dependency) arrows\n6. Use text to describe arrows\n7. Zoom System box: users, interacting systems retained\n8. Model server side / client side boxes, think in terms of deployable containers. Show Applications, APIs and UIs, Data Stores (e.g. DB)\n9. Zoom each Container box: draw Components: surrounding Containers retained\n\n\n\n*) Note: C4 doesn't limit for notation - it is about abstraction layers. So it's free to use UML or any other notation where you need\n\n*) Layers, Subsystems - modeled by grouping of components. Specifically for huge Monoliths subsystems (Maven modules inside Monolith) - are modeled via grouping\n\n*) Note: C4 site has tooling \"Structurizer\" for C4 modelling. And many modelling cases reviewed on C4 site.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
